<div class="profile-header">
  <figure class="profile-photo">
    <img src="/blog/jingtao-li.jpg" alt="Portrait of Jingtao Li" />
  </figure>
  <div class="profile-intro">
    <p class="profile-label">New Faces</p>
    <p>Jingtao Li's research interests lie in Earth vision interpretation, with a particular focus on anomaly detection and foundation model techniques for remote sensing imagery.</p>
  </div>
</div>

At Tessera, he is interested in working to improve the representation quality of the model and explore its downstream application potential, with the broader goal of contributing to global sustainable development.

<blockquote class="pull-quote pending">
  <p>[Quote pending — awaiting Li's answer to the standard prompt.]</p>
</blockquote>

Li earned his PhD from Wuhan University, supervised by Yanfei Zhong and Liangpei Zhang. He joins the University of Cambridge Department of Computer Science & Technology as a research associate.

---

